WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.470
In 1971, the census counted over
seven million people in London.

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.160
By 1981, the estimate had
fallen to six million,

3
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.230
eight hundred and five thousand.

4
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.330
London was shrinking.

5
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.110
Then it turned.

6
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.230
By 2025: over nine point one million.

7
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.330
Meanwhile, in the North East,
the population has barely grown.

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.460
So why has London boomed, while
the North East has barely grown?

9
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.790
In this mission, you'll break
population change into its parts:

10
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.270
births, deaths, and
people moving in and out.

11
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.170
Then you'll follow who
moves where, by age,

12
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.410
from inner city to countryside.

13
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: explain why London has
grown so much faster than the North East.
